---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, issueUrl } from '../lib/site.js';
import { author, breadcrumbs } from '../lib/jsonld.js';
---

<Base
  ogImage="/og/pages/about.png"
  title="About"
  description="Who maintains the Africa Compute Tracker, why it exists, and how to get in touch or contribute a correction."
  schema={[
    { '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': `${SITE.url}/about/`, url: `${SITE.url}/about/`, name: 'About the Africa Compute Tracker', mainEntity: author },
    breadcrumbs([['Home', '/'], ['About', '/about/']]),
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-prose pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">About the tracker</h1>

    <div class="md mt-6 text-[1.0625rem]">
      <p>
        Africa is in the middle of an AI infrastructure announcement cycle. Hyperscalers, colocation providers and
        "AI factory" ventures are promising hundreds of megawatts of new capacity, often in places where the grid is
        already strained. Announcements are easy to find. What has actually been built, how much power it draws and
        who owns it are much harder to pin down.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Africa Compute Tracker is an attempt to keep that record straight. Each facility is a plain text file in a
        public repository. Every figure carries a source, a trust tier, a retrieval date and a confidence level.
        Contested assertions are kept apart from sourced facts, and the maintainer's own judgement is labelled as such.
      </p>

      <h2>Who maintains it</h2>
      <p>
        The tracker is built and maintained by <a href="https://tawanda.dev/" rel="author">Tawanda Moyo</a>, a software engineer
        and technical writer in Harare working on AI safety, with a focus on compute governance.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Found an error? <a href={issueUrl('source-correction')}>Report a correction</a>. Corrections are handled first.</li>
        <li>Know of a facility that should be here? <a href={issueUrl('new-facility-lead')}>Suggest it</a> with a source.</li>
        <li>Using the data, or want to collaborate? <a href={issueUrl('data-use')}>Open a conversation</a> or reach out via <a href="https://tawanda.dev/about/">tawanda.dev</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What it is not</h2>
      <p>
        This is not a complete census. It covers hyperscale, large colocation and purpose-built AI facilities, and it
        favours fewer, well-sourced records over many thin ones. A facility's absence means it has not been recorded
        yet. See the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> for scope and sourcing rules, and the
        <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a> for what has changed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
